hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18084","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah from Amr ibn Maymun from Abdullah ibn Rabiah from Ubayd ibn Khalid al-Sulami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between two men, then one of them was killed and the other died after him, then we prayed over him, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What did you say. They said: We supplicated for him: O Allah, join him to his companion. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then where is his prayer after his prayer, and where is his fasting after his fasting, and where is his deed after his deed, Shubah doubted in the prayer and the deed, in one of them, that between them as between the heaven and the earth."
"18085","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Amr ibn Maymun narrating from Abdullah ibn Rabiah al-Sulami from Ubayd ibn Khalid, and he was among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between two men, then he mentioned the hadith."
"18086","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Ibn Murrah narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Maymun from Abdullah ibn Rabiah from Ubayd ibn Khalid, a man from Banu Sulaym, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between two men, then one of them was killed and the other died after him, then we prayed over him, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What did you say. They said: We supplicated for him to forgive him and have mercy upon him and join him to his companion. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then where is his prayer after his prayer, and his deed after his deed, or his fasting after his fasting. He said: What is between them as between the heaven and the earth."
"18087","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to me from Tamim ibn Salamah, or Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Ubayd ibn Khalid al-Sulami, and he was among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Sudden death is a seizure of wrath."
"18088","And he narrated it once from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"18089","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Mansur from Tamim ibn Salamah from Ubayd ibn Khalid al-Sulami, and he was among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Concerning sudden death, a seizure of wrath."
